Package: precisionenvelope
Type: Package
Title: Sharp Precision Envelopes for Outcomes Missing at Random
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Satoshi", "Nakamura", , "s-nakamura@med.mie-u.ac.jp", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes the range of precision that can survive when an outcome
    or an all-or-none block of variables is missing at random. For a stated
    overall observation rate and a lower bound on the observation
    probability, the package returns the smallest and largest efficient
    variance that any admissible missingness mechanism can produce, the
    corresponding information retention and standard error inflation, and
    whether a precision requirement is guaranteed, depends on the
    allocation of missingness, or cannot be met. It also plans
    minimum-cost targeted recovery of missing outcomes, and estimates the
    envelope from data on a partially observed continuous outcome by
    cross-fitted one-step estimation with a refitted bootstrap band over a
    prespecified grid of observation rates. The method is described in
    Nakamura (2026) <doi:10.3390/stats9050110>.
